{
  "_comment": [
    "CH06-SIGNER-IMPERSONATION registry: which signing certificates may claim a",
    "protected bank package name. Keyed by the official Play Store package for",
    "each of the ten institutions in the banking baseline corpus (BASE-01-SBI",
    "through BASE-10-UNION); the same list lives in code at",
    "shared/sudarshan_core/engines/vide/official_packages.py.",
    "",
    "allowed_signers_sha256 holds the SHA-256 fingerprints of the certificates",
    "the genuine app is signed with. An EMPTY list is meaningful, not missing",
    "data: it means no canonical fingerprint has been provisioned for that",
    "package yet, so ANY APK claiming it is treated as impersonation. That is",
    "the conservative reading and matches the rule VIDE enforces - a package",
    "name is an identity claim, and an unverifiable claim is not a valid one.",
    "",
    "Populate these from Play Store signing certificates before deploying",
    "against real-world traffic, or genuine bank apps will be flagged. Set",
    "signers_provisioned to true once a package's fingerprints are filled in."
  ],
